# Discharge Patient Flow

Discharge owns the final inpatient clearance sequence on the IPD admission; keep planning, summary, medicines, billing, nursing sign-off, bed release, and closure in one controlled path.

## Stage Sequence

- Doctor marks discharge as planned.
- Pending orders and results are reviewed.
- Discharge summary and follow-up are prepared.
- Pharmacy prepares take-home medicines.
- Billing completes final settlement or insurance closure.
- Nursing completes clearance and patient education.
- Patient exits and the bed is released for cleaning.
- IPD encounter is finalized and closed.

## Handoffs

- Doctor owns discharge decision and summary.
- Pharmacy owns take-home medicine readiness.
- Billing owns financial settlement only.
- Ward nurse owns clearance and education.
- Bed manager or housekeeping owns bed release after exit.

## Hard Invariants

- Must not conflate OPD `DISCHARGED` with IPD discharge.
- Must not mark the patient discharged until IPD closure is complete.
- Must not skip required pharmacy, billing, or nursing clearance.
- Must not use discharge to execute unrelated inpatient care.

## Allowed Critical Actions

- Show pending items early so staff can clear blockers before exit.
- Keep `DISCHARGE_PLANNED` distinct from final `DISCHARGED`.
- Link to the billing workspace instead of duplicating payment logic.
- Trigger bed release only after the patient has physically left.

